      "description": "Watch Monza vs Udinese highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. On August 29, 2026, Monza and Udinese locked horns in a Serie A clash that promised tactical intrigue and high-octane football. With both sides eager to climb the table, the stage was set for a confrontation where momentum would shift with every passing minute. A Chaotic Opening Period The match ignited in the 32nd minute when a defensive lapse by Mathis Mout gifted the visitors an opening. Jakub Piotrowski made no mistake, firing home with his left foot after being set up by Hassane Kamara . Monza ’s response was swift and clinical. Just five minutes later, Andrea Colpani leveled the scores with a well-placed right-footed finish, following a sequence involving Patrick Cutrone and a decisive pass from Ricardo Mangas . As the first half drew to a close, Udinese unleashed a devastating double blow that left the home crowd stunned. In the 45th minute, Hassane Kamara capitalized on a poor clearance from goalkeeper Demba Thiam to strike from distance. Deep into stoppage time (45+3'), Jurgen Ekkelenkamp extended the lead further, rifling a shot into the net from outside the box after a corner delivered by Unai Gomez . This rapid-fire sequence gave the visitors a commanding cushion heading into the interval. Monza’s Late Surge and Defensive Resilience The second half saw Monza emerge with renewed purpose, pushing high to salvage a result. Their persistence paid off in the 63rd minute when Gustavo Varela rose highest to head home an Ebenezer Akinsanmiro cross, cutting the deficit to a single goal. The atmosphere intensified as the home side threw everything forward, forcing the Udinese backline into a series of desperate clearances. In a frantic final ten minutes, Monza came agonizingly close to an equalizer. Andrea Carboni saw his header saved comfortably by Maduka Okoye , who remained a pillar of stability for the visitors. As the clock ticked into the 94th minute, Michael Folorunsho had one final chance to steal a point, but his effort whistled wide of the target. Udinese held firm under immense pressure to secure a hard-fought victory in a contest that defined the competitive spirit of Italian football."
