      "description": "Watch Udinese vs Cagliari highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 19, 2026. The Serie A stage was set for an intriguing tactical battle as Udinese welcomed Cagliari in a clash defined by missed opportunities and a single moment of brilliance. Both sides entered the fray with high energy, looking to carve out an early advantage in a contest that stayed balanced on a knife-edge for long periods. A Physical Opening Exchange Taking place on September 19, 2026 , the match began with a flurry of intensity from the home side. Udinese attempted to stamp their authority early on, though their aggression resulted in yellow cards for Nicolo Zaniolo and Jesper Karlstroem within the first 25 minutes. Despite the disciplinary setbacks, the hosts dominated the aerial battle, with Mergim Vojvoda delivering several dangerous corners. However, Cagliari goalkeeper Elia Caprile proved to be an unbeatable wall in the first half, comfortably saving two goalbound headers from Idrissa Gueye to keep the scores level. Maldini Finds the Breakthrough The deadlock was finally broken in the 54th minute through a lapse in the Udinese defense. A mix-up involving Christian Kabasele and James Abankwah gifted an opening to Daniel Maldini , who made no mistake. Displaying composure, Maldini unleashed a clinical left-footed strike that found the back of the net, giving Cagliari a precious lead against the run of play. The goal forced the hosts into a series of tactical changes, including the introduction of Giorgi Chakvetadze and Vakoun Issouf Bayo to bolster the attack. Late Pressure and Resilient Defense As the clock ticked toward full-time, Udinese threw everything forward, maintaining a staggering 70% of ball possession. They pushed the Cagliari backline to its limits, but the visitors remained disciplined under pressure. Bayo came agonizingly close to an equalizer in the 89th minute, but his effort drifted wide of the target. In a frantic period of stoppage time, Cagliari managed to neutralize every threat, including a late foul by Gueye on Caprile , ensuring they headed home with all three points after a resilient defensive display."
